{"step_index":11507,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T15:30:37Z","thinking":"The byte size reported by the initial method matches the output of a different utility, confirming its accuracy. This method efficiently determines the exact byte size, file count, and folder count within a single execution. The process avoids redundant directory traversals, and efficiently handles potential permission errors.\n\n\nInvestigating the appropriate timeout duration for directory size calculations, especially for large directories, is crucial. A 3.5-second timeout proved insufficient for a directory with 882,672 files, leading to possible timeouts and subsequent caching of erroneous results. Increasing the timeout to 7 or 8 seconds should accommodate larger directories and prevent premature termination, ensuring accurate results are cached. Addressing the UI's user experience involves aligning the timeout duration with the frontend's modal, displaying a spinner while the operation executes and then caching the results.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport subprocess, time\n\ndef format_size(size_bytes):\n    if size_bytes is None:\n        return 'Unknown'\n    if size_bytes < 1024:\n        return f'{size_bytes} B'\n    elif size_bytes < 1024 * 1024:\n        return f'{size_bytes / 1024:.1f} KB'\n    elif size_bytes < 1024 * 1024 * 1024:\n        return f'{size_bytes / (1024 * 1024):.2f} MB'\n    else:\n        return f'{size_bytes / (1024 * 1024 * 1024):.2f} GB'\n\ndef calc_properties(target_path, timeout=8.0):\n    t0 = time.time()\n    try:\n        # Run single find command with size (%s) and type (%y)\n        p = subprocess.run(\n            ['find', target_path, '-mindepth', '1', '-printf', '%s %y\\n'],\n            capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout\n        )\n        lines = p.stdout.splitlines()\n        total_bytes = 0\n        files_count = 0\n        folders_count = 0\n        for line in lines:\n            parts = line.split()\n            if len(parts) == 2:\n                sz, t = parts\n                if t != 'd':\n                    try:\n                        total_bytes += int(sz)\n                    except:\n                        pass\n                    files_count += 1\n                else:\n                    folders_count += 1\n        \n        t1 = time.time()\n        return {\n            'success': True,\n            'time': round(t1 - t0, 3),\n            'size_bytes': total_bytes,\n            'size_str': format_size(total_bytes),\n            'size_bytes_formatted': f'{total_bytes:,} bytes',\n            'files_count': files_count,\n            'folders_count': folders_count,\n            'contains_str': f'{files_count:,} Files, {folders_count:,} Folders'\n        }\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n        # If even 8s times out, fall back to fast du\n        try:\n            p_du = subprocess.run(['du', '-sb', target_path], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=3.0)\n            if p_du.stdout:\n                last_line = p_du.stdout.strip().splitlines()[-1]\n                sz = int(last_line.split()[0])\n                return {\n                    'success': True,\n                    'size_bytes': sz,\n                    'size_str': format_size(sz),\n                    'size_bytes_formatted': f'{sz:,} bytes',\n                    'files_count': 0,\n                    'folders_count': 0,\n                    'contains_str': 'Large directory (file count skipped)'\n                }\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        return {'success': False, 'error': 'Timeout'}\n\nprint(calc_properties('/home/azureuser'))\n\"","Cwd":"/home/azureuser/IrakIroan/azure_file_explorer","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":15000,"toolAction":"Testing optimized calc_properties","toolSummary":"Test calc_properties on /home/azureuser"}}]}
